Decode extractor clips with PyAV directly, producing identical tensors.

WLASLDataset spends ~0.5 s per clip in pytorchvideo's EncodedVideo (BytesIO
copy, per-frame to_rgb + from_numpy), which caps training at ~11 clips/s on
an H100 that sustains 24. decode_clip selects the same frames by the same
rule (pts in [ceil(0), ceil(end_sec)) in the stream's time base, deduplicated
and sorted) and converts with the same FFmpeg, in ~0.2 s. Verified
bit-identical to the original on real clips before use (see README).

